<p>President Trump said on April 10 that the United States will have the Strait of Hormuz &quot;open fairly soon,&quot; while acknowledging that doing so &quot;won&#x27;t be easy&quot; as Washington and Iran head toward talks over the vital waterway. He also said the US would not accept what Al Jazeera described as Iran&#x27;s imposition of a de facto toll system in the strait, one of the world&#x27;s most important energy transit routes. The comments suggest a possible diplomatic opening after severe disruption to global energy supplies linked to Tehran&#x27;s blockade since the start of the Iran war, as described by The Hindu. Trump also said other countries that use the strait were offering help, though he did not name them, a sign that the issue is drawing broader international attention as governments look for a way to restore shipping through the corridor.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/yudSwWXwsPnXH5Avp2O7W5nO3V0EUaual4lRchG3wBzbZ0mj6g5RWwJJP9z0yhiuIwH2-zmjWGkHt3wfGxzOvpVPyvxmo4rzIHN7ebXx030188dMIgiBOnikqZBAadNv5IAJlJbvQMIf0SRJZ0wj0mBYsuMLkmTaz1Nhs-4ZI041pk1n6JJcLIHl1kmydRfUsVMRQhx97Yyxom02UmJOj00AZHXEiSe6dol_Pj4hkRkxNUaGo6T3bnY' alt='President Donald Trump speaks to reporters as he says the US will have the Strait of Hormuz open fairly soon.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Military hint: Trump said, &quot;We&#x27;re going to open up the gulf with or without them... or the strait as they call it,&quot; signaling that Washington was considering steps beyond negotiations if needed.</li><li>Shared reliance: Trump stressed that &quot;other countries use the strait&quot; and said those countries were stepping forward to help, pointing to a broader coalition interest in restoring passage.</li><li>Energy shock: The Hindu described the disruption caused by Tehran&#x27;s blockade as the worst interruption to global energy supplies in history, underscoring why reopening the waterway has become urgent.</li></ul><blockquote>It won&#x27;t be easy... I would say this - we will have that open fairly soon - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Donald Trump: Trump said the United States would have the strait open fairly soon but warned that the effort would be difficult, while also saying other countries were ready to help. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/trump-says-us-will-have-strait-of-hormuz-open-fairly-soon'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Iran: Al Jazeera reported that Tehran has effectively imposed a toll-like system in the strait and has maintained a blockade there since the start of the war, shaping the current confrontation. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2026/4/11/trump-says-strait-of-hormuz-to-reopen-soon-as-us-iran-head-to-talks'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>The Hindu&#x27;s coverage: The Hindu framed the blockade as a historic shock to global energy flows, emphasizing the scale of the supply disruption rather than just the diplomatic maneuvering. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-says-us-will-have-strait-of-hormuz-open-fairly-soon/article70849173.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2026/4/11/trump-says-strait-of-hormuz-to-reopen-soon-as-us-iran-head-to-talks'>Trump says Strait of Hormuz to reopen ‘soon’ as US, Iran head to talks</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/trump-says-us-will-have-strait-of-hormuz-open-fairly-soon'>Trump says US will have Strait of Hormuz ‘open fairly soon’</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/trump-says-us-will-have-strait-hormuz-open-fairly-soon'>Trump says US will have Strait of Hormuz &#x27;open fairly soon&#x27;</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-says-us-will-have-strait-of-hormuz-open-fairly-soon/article70849173.ece'>Trump says U.S. will have Strait of Hormuz &#x27;open fairly soo